# Amazon through HasData

Five tools. `amazon_search_getSearchResults` takes a query, the other four take an identifier: `asin` for a product or its reviews, `sellerId` for a seller or that seller's catalogue.

## Identifiers are marketplace-scoped

`domain` decides which Amazon you are reading, and an ASIN that exists on `www.amazon.com` often does not exist on `www.amazon.de`. The same goes for a seller id. When a lookup fails, check the domain before you decide the item is gone.

## Destination changes the answer

`deliveryZip` and `shippingLocation` shift availability, price and the seller mix, not just the delivery line. A price comparison across locations is only honest if you pass the location deliberately and say which one you used.

## Reading the payload

A search that matches nothing returns a successful result with an empty `productResults` array, so branch on length rather than waiting for an error. A live listing can come back without a usable `currentPrice` when the item is out of stock or sold only through other sellers, so treat the price as optional and say so instead of printing zero.

The reviews tool pages and filters: `stars`, `reviewerType`, `mediaType` and `sortBy` narrow the set at no extra cost, which beats pulling everything and filtering afterwards.
